    description: "Defer consequential choices made in 'hot' visceral states (anger, arousal, craving, panic) until you cool down, and precommit while calm. Ariely & Loewenstein showed that under sexual arousal, young men's stated willingness to take risks and cross moral lines rose dramatically, and crucially they could not predict this shift when cold, evidence for a systematic hot-cold empathy gap that a waiting period neutralizes.",
