    description: "SPRINT (n=9,361 higher-risk adults without diabetes) randomized systolic targets of <120 vs <140 mmHg. Intensive control cut major cardiovascular events by about 25% and all-cause mortality by about 27%, with a number-needed-to-treat around 61 to prevent one primary-outcome event over ~3.3 years — one of the strongest preventive effects in medicine.",
    callout: "Educational, not medical advice; discuss with a clinician. Intensive targets raised rates of hypotension, syncope, electrolyte abnormalities and acute kidney injury; SPRINT used standardized unattended measurement that reads several mmHg lower than a typical office cuff, so its numbers don't translate 1:1 to a clinic reading.",
