    description: "Anxiety that spikes specifically around evaluation depresses performance across GPA, university entrance exams, and standardized/aptitude tests. Von der Embse and colleagues' 30-year meta-analytic review of 238 studies found test anxiety negatively related to a wide range of performance outcomes with small-to-medium effect sizes, most pronounced in the middle-school years, and most tightly linked to low self-esteem and self-efficacy. The worry component consumes attention that would otherwise go to the task.",
