    description: "Languishing is a state of low subjective, psychological, and social well-being in the ABSENCE of diagnosable illness — feeling empty, stagnant, and 'meh' rather than sick. In Keyes's MIDUS data (n=3,032), languishing adults carried roughly double the risk of a 12-month major depressive episode compared with the moderately mentally healthy, and languishing was associated with the worst psychosocial functioning short of depression itself. Prospectively, people who declined toward or stayed in languishing had markedly higher incidence of later mental illness than those who gained or kept positive mental health.",
