    description: "Anorexia nervosa carries among the highest mortality of any mental disorder. A 2026 meta-analysis (Lai et al.; 22 studies, 33,176 patients) reported a pooled standardized mortality ratio of 5.06 (95% CI 3.47–7.38), with suicide and cardiac events accounting for ~21% and ~19% of deaths. The classic Arcelus et al. (2011) meta-analysis of 36 studies found an AN SMR of 5.86. Starvation drives cardiac, bone, endocrine, and neurocognitive damage alongside acute suicide risk.",
    callout: "SMRs vary widely by cohort severity and follow-up length (inpatient samples inflate estimates), and some organ damage is reversible with sustained weight restoration — the mortality figure is a ceiling from the sickest, longest-followed populations, not every case.",
