    description: "When an institution a person depends on (a university, employer, military, or church) fails to prevent harm or responds callously after it, the mishandling compounds the original injury. Smith & Freyd (2013) found that institutional betrayal following sexual assault independently predicted worse anxiety, dissociation, and sexual-trauma symptoms beyond the assault itself. Later work links institutional betrayal to elevated physical health complaints and dissociation even after controlling for interpersonal betrayal-trauma exposure.",
