    harm: { severity: 2, onset: "immediate", reversibility: "recovers" },
    degrades: ["self-esteem", "closure and sense-making", "trust in future relationships", "emotional regulation"],
    description: "Ghosting — ending a relationship by abruptly vanishing with no explanation — leaves the recipient without the closure needed to make sense of the loss, breeding self-blame and rumination. Early studies report elevated anxiety and lowered self-esteem, and comparative work (Pancani et al., 2022; and dissolution-strategy studies) suggests ghosting produces worse outcomes than a direct rejection because ambiguity blocks resolution. Victims cycle through surprise/confusion, then guilt/anger/sadness, before acceptance.",
