    feeds: ["Orderly wealth transfer", "Family protection", "Avoiding probate cost and delay"],
    description: "A valid will directs asset distribution and names guardians for minors; without one, state intestacy law and probate court decide, often slowly and publicly. Critically, beneficiary designations on retirement accounts, life insurance, and TOD/POD accounts pass outside the will and override it. The U.S. Supreme Court confirmed the named beneficiary controls even against a contrary divorce waiver (Kennedy v. Plan Administrator for DuPont Savings Plan, 2009). Keeping designations current after marriage, divorce, or a birth is as important as the will itself.",
