    description: "A personal umbrella policy adds $1-10M of liability coverage on top of auto and home limits, paying (plus legal-defense costs) when a judgment exceeds the underlying policy. Because premiums are low relative to coverage, often a few hundred dollars per $1M, it is an efficient transfer of the rare catastrophic-lawsuit risk that could otherwise reach savings, home equity, and future wages. Insurers typically require high underlying auto/home liability limits (often $250k-$300k) as a condition.",
