    description: "Medical bills are error-prone and negotiable. In a nationally representative survey (Duffy et al., JAMA Health Forum, 2024), among people who contacted a billing office about a problematic bill, about 74% who flagged an error had it corrected, about 76% who cited unaffordability received some relief, and roughly 62% who tried to negotiate got the price dropped. The main tactics: request an itemized bill, check it against the insurer's Explanation of Benefits, and ask for financial assistance or self-pay rates. The federal No Surprises Act (2022) also blocks many out-of-network balance bills.",
