    impact: { magnitude: 4, latency: "months", durability: "lasting", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["identity continuity through life transitions", "diversified social support", "sense of meaning and purpose", "buffer against depression and loneliness"],
    description: "Belonging to several meaningful social groups (clubs, teams, faith, volunteer, hobby) supplies identity, support, and meaning — the 'social cure'. Longitudinal cohorts show that maintaining multiple group memberships across major transitions (e.g., retirement) predicts lower mortality risk and better quality of life; losing memberships raises risk. 'Groups 4 Health'-style interventions that rebuild group ties show reduced depression and loneliness.",
