    impact: { magnitude: 3, latency: "months", durability: "lasting", effort: "moderate" },
    feeds: ["generalized trust and reciprocity", "access to civic and instrumental resources", "collective efficacy", "sense of civic belonging"],
    description: "Active participation in voluntary associations, civic groups, and reciprocal community networks (Putnam's social capital) is consistently linked to better self-rated health and lower mortality. A systematic review of reviews found individual and area social capital positively associated with health; a meta-analysis of 39 studies found social capital raised odds of good health ~27%, with trust (+32%) and reciprocity (+39%) strongest.",
    callout: "Heavily confounded by socioeconomic status, personality, and baseline health, and social-capital measures are inconsistent across studies; some 'bonding' capital can also be exclusionary or harmful. Treat associational membership as a correlate with modest, hard-to-isolate causal weight.",
