    description: "Ray Oldenburg's 'third places' (cafes, pubs, barbershops, libraries, gyms — neutral, accessible spots beyond home and work) host the low-stakes, repeated, voluntary encounters that build belonging and weak-tie networks. Observational work links greater neighborhood availability of third places to lower loneliness (e.g., among caregiving spouses) and higher social capital. The mechanism is exposure to unplanned, recurring, obligation-free contact rather than any single 'dose'.",
