    degrades: ["Strategic patience", "Disciplined non-intervention", "Over-trading / over-treatment avoidance", "Regret-resistant decision-making"],
    description: "The mirror of omission bias: in situations where waiting is optimal, people feel compelled to 'do something.' Bar-Eli et al. analyzed 286 elite penalty kicks and found goalkeepers almost always dive left or right even though staying centered stops more shots — because a goal conceded while standing still feels worse than one conceded while diving. The same norm-driven urge shows up as over-trading, over-treatment in medicine, and over-managing.",
