    description: "Clark's cognitive model holds that panic attacks arise when benign arousal sensations (palpitations, dizziness) are catastrophically misread as signs of imminent death, madness, or collapse — a positive-feedback loop that escalates arousal into panic. A systematic review/meta-analysis found medium-to-large differences in catastrophic misinterpretation between panic-disorder patients and both healthy controls and other anxiety patients, supporting it as relatively specific to panic. Cognitive therapy targeting these misinterpretations is highly effective.",
