    description: "Cheating is socially contagious: seeing a peer transgress with impunity shifts the perceived descriptive norm and increases one's own dishonesty — but seeing an out-group member do it, or having the possibility of cheating made salient, can decrease it (Gino, Ayal & Ariely, 2009). Unethical behavior thus tracks the implied norms of one's reference group more than a rational cost-benefit calculation, which is how corrupt cultures normalize and spread wrongdoing.",
