    description: "When leaders celebrate and promote the people who heroically rescue last-minute crises, the organization systematically under-invests in prevention. Repenning and Sterman's system-dynamics work models this as a 'capability trap': low process capability creates fires, fires consume all the time that improvement would need, and rewarding firefighting perpetuates the cycle through self-confirming attribution errors. The result is chronic overload and eroding capability that looks locally rational at every step.",
