    description: "Interfaces engineered without natural stopping cues — infinite scroll, autoplay, pull-to-refresh — remove the decision points where a user would otherwise stop, producing longer, more automatic sessions and post-use regret. HCI work on 'attention-capture deceptive designs' catalogs these patterns and links them to users losing track of goals, time, and control, exploiting mechanisms like variable reward and the Zeigarnik effect.",
