    description: "Chronic emptiness — a persistent sense of hollowness, disconnection from self and others, and purposelessness — is increasingly framed as a transdiagnostic risk factor rather than a mere depression symptom. Qualitative and psychometric work distinguishes it from loneliness, hopelessness, dissociation and depression, and sufferers often trace it to 'everything feels meaningless' or 'I have no purpose,' with the feeling directly linked to suicidal ideation. It is associated with self-harm, suicidality and impaired social and vocational functioning, retaining incremental validity after controlling for personality pathology and current distress.",
