    description: "Higgins's self-discrepancy theory holds that gaps between one's actual self and one's ideal self breed dejection-related emotions (sadness, disappointment), while gaps from the ought self breed agitation (anxiety, guilt). A 70-study meta-analysis (Mason et al., 2019) confirms self-discrepancy has a small-to-medium, robust transdiagnostic association with psychopathology — but the neat ideal→depression / ought→anxiety specificity was NOT supported; both discrepancies predict both.",
