    description: "Interpersonal accuracy — correctly reading faces, voice, and body for others' states — is a measurable skill (e.g., PONS, DANVA) that predicts real outcomes; being poor at it means missing the affective signals that steer interaction. Reviews link higher nonverbal decoding accuracy to better workplace and relationship results, and emotion-recognition ability predicts negotiation effectiveness and even income. Weak decoders talk past people's discomfort, disinterest, or upset, producing awkwardness, mistrust, and avoidable conflict.",
