    degrades: ["working memory and processing speed", "emotional stability and mood", "social connection (via stigma and disclosure fear)", "medication adherence and self-management"],
    description: "Modern combination antiretroviral therapy (cART) has made life expectancy near-normal for treated people living with HIV, but the disease becomes a lifelong burden rather than a resolved event. HIV-associated neurocognitive disorder (HAND) persists even after viral suppression — pooled prevalence estimates run high (~40%+), though today it is dominated by mild/asymptomatic forms rather than dementia. Stigma, depression, and accelerated non-AIDS comorbidities (cardiovascular, bone, frailty) compound the load and erode adherence and quality of life.",
    callout: "The scary older HAND prevalence figures predate suppressive cART and conflate mild asymptomatic impairment with disabling dementia; on effective treatment, severe forms are now uncommon and life expectancy approaches normal.",
