    description: "Fibromyalgia — chronic widespread pain with fatigue, unrefreshing sleep, and cognitive difficulty ('fibro fog') — has a worldwide mean point prevalence near 2.7% (range 0.4–9.3%), about three times more common in women. It is now understood as a central sensitization / nociplastic pain state rather than joint or muscle damage. Self-reported disability runs 10–30%, with large hits to quality of life, productivity, and daily function even under treatment.",
