    degrades: ["fine motor control and grip strength", "manual dexterity", "self-care and daily tasks", "hand appearance"],
    description: "Symptomatic hand OA affects roughly 13–26% of adults (higher in women, rising with age) and erodes the fine end of bodily capacity: pinch and grip strength fall, joints stiffen and deform, and tasks like buttoning, opening jars, and writing become painful. It is a distinct burden from knee/hip OA because it targets dexterity and manual work rather than mobility, and visible nodal deformities add an appearance dimension.",
