    description: "Traumatic SCI imposes one of the highest per-person economic burdens in medicine: systematic reviews estimate lifetime costs of roughly US$1.5M–$3.0M, with first-year mean costs reaching ~US$1M, and costs markedly higher for cervical (tetraplegia) than thoracic injuries. A 67-study systematic review (Diop & Epstein, 2024) found health-related quality of life is substantially reduced, especially on physical dimensions, and worsens with higher neurological level. Onset is immediate and paralysis is typically permanent.",
