    degrades: ["Physical mobility and function", "Body image", "Emotional wellbeing", "Employment and earning capacity", "Independent daily functioning"],
    description: "Traumatic limb loss carries a heavy dual burden of psychiatric morbidity and chronic pain. A 61-study meta-analysis (Singh et al., 2024; 9,852 amputees) found a pooled depression prevalence of ~34% (higher in middle-income settings), while a separate meta-analysis (Limakatso et al., 2020) found roughly 6 in 10 amputees report phantom limb pain. Grief, altered body image, low self-esteem, and phantom/residual-limb pain interlink with anxiety, PTSD, sleep disturbance, and suicidal ideation. Onset is immediate and the loss is permanent.",
