    description: "Vertebral fractures are the most common fragility fracture (>1.4 million/year worldwide) yet are widely under-recognized. A meta-analysis of 16 observational studies (Al-Sari et al., 2016) found a clear association between vertebral fracture and worse physical health-related quality of life after adjusting for age. These fractures also signal markedly elevated risk of future fractures and excess mortality, with persistent back pain, progressive kyphosis, and functional decline. Onset can be immediate (traumatic) or insidious; recovery is partial.",
