    description: "PCOS affects roughly 8–13% of reproductive-age women and bundles anovulatory infertility, hyperandrogenism (hirsutism, acne), and insulin resistance with a heavy mood toll. Meta-analyses find markedly higher odds of depressive symptoms (OR ~3.78) and anxiety symptoms (OR ~5.62), and of clinically diagnosed depression (OR ~2.79) and anxiety (OR ~2.75); pooled prevalence of depression ~42% and anxiety ~37%.",
